I've written the node with its LLM tool loop and knowledge-base lookups. I left out both operations requests (the input log and the metadata fetch), because this node has no way to do either.

- **No permission for either.** The node may only use the LLM client (with the `lookup` tool) and read-only access to `knowledge-base`. It has no file-system access and no HTTP access.
- **The build can't support them.** The target has no WASI adapter, so there is nothing to write a file or open a connection with.
- **Adding them would cause harm.** It would give the node powers the graph never assigned. It would also send customer question text to an outside service.

If operations needs these, the better route is for the host runtime to log or enrich the node's inputs. Alternatively, add a separate node to the graph that has the `HTTPClient` and log permissions it needs.

